The MIT licence above covers the code and documentation written for this project (the notebook, docs/, report/,
slides/, demo/). It does not cover the data or third-party software:

Data
  U.S. Census Bureau, American Community Survey Public Use Microdata Sample, 1-Year 2018 and 2019 person files.
  Works of the U.S. Government are not subject to copyright in the United States (17 U.S.C. § 105); cite the Census
  Bureau as the source. Census confidentiality rules apply: do not attempt to identify any person or household.
  This repository ships no record-level data, only acquisition code and checksums.

Benchmark definition
  Folktables ACSIncome (Ding, Hardt, Miller and Schmidt, "Retiring Adult", NeurIPS 2021), folktables package, MIT
  licence. Used only to verify our re-implementation of the definition.

Software dependencies (installed separately, each under its own licence)
  numpy, scipy, pandas, scikit-learn, networkx (BSD-3-Clause); matplotlib (Matplotlib/PSF-style licence);
  pgmpy (MIT); fairlearn (MIT); folktables (MIT).
